    "updated_at": "2023-12-05T13:59:18Z",
    "body": "Is there much value left in using ANGLE over OpenGL as opposed to just native OpenGL? The main rationale for using ANGLE on macOS was the fear that bitrotting OpenGL drivers would have too many issues, but if we're still using them via ANGLE there might not be much benefit in having ANGLE at all?\r\n\r\nOn the other hand if there we still want to have ANGLE over Metal as an opt-in for devices with proper Metal support, we could still considering #84563. But it sounds like ANGLE over Metal has core issues even on latest macOS?",
